a former kansas city chiefs assistant  coach is facing possible prison time  after a car accident  that critically injured a five-year-old  girl in february yesterday brit reed  the son of head coach andy reed was  charged with driving while intoxicated  resulting in serious physical injury  erika duncan spoke to the attorney for  the little girl's family after the  charges were announced  along this kansas city highway just  three days before the chiefs took the  field in super bowl 55  a severe car crash left five-year-old  ariel young  critically injured a voicemail captured  her mother's frantic screams  but ariel was unresponsive in the back  seat of her mother's totaled suv  according to the police report britt  reed was driving nearly 20 miles over  the speed limit  when he struck that suv and another  vehicle parked on the side of the  highway  officers said they smelled alcohol on  reed and his eyes were bloodshot  he admitted to having two to three  drinks and taking adderall before  driving  tess revealed he had a blood alcohol  content of  .113 which is over the legal driving  limit  ariel was in a coma for 11 days and  suffered skull fractures  and brain injuries which the family now  fears could be permanent  since the february 4th crash ariel has  not  walked she has not talked and she cannot  eat and she's dependent upon a feeding  tube  for basic nutrition attorney tom porto  represents the family  the result was what we've been asking  for and that's the most serious charge  that could be filed against brit reed at  the time of the crash britt reed was an  assistant coach for the kansas city  chiefs  his father andy reid is the team's head  coach  and spoke about the incident after their  super bowl loss  my heart goes out to all those that were  involved in the accident in particular  the family  with the little girl who's fighting for  her life porto says he expects to file  civil litigation if any entity be it  read personally  be it the chiefs as an organization is  responsible for the damage that was done  to this five-year-old  absolutely we will be pursuing them
 

